1. Overview
The Orthotic Charger is a wireless charging system designed to recharge orthotic device batteries via inductive coupling. The system uses a parallel resonant transmitter coil configuration driven by an ATTiny1616 microcontroller, with USB-C power input and LED status indication.

2. Circuit Design
2.1 Power Supply
USB-C input via USB4120-03-C connector with CC1/CC2 pull-down resistors (5.1kΩ)

200mA resettable fuse (F1) for overcurrent protection

Ferrite bead (BLM18KG471) for EMI filtering

ESD protection via D5V0L1B2WS TVS diode

Schottky diode (PMEG6010CEJ) for reverse polarity protection

2.2 Coil Driver
P-channel MOSFET (DMG2305UX) as high-side switch (Q1)

Dual N-channel MOSFETs (DMN2046U) for low-side drive (Q2, Q3 - DNF)

Flyback diode (BAS16XV2T5G) for coil protection

100µF bulk capacitors (C6, C8) for energy storage

2.3 Sensing & Feedback
ADC_VBUS: USB voltage monitoring via resistor divider (R5/R6: 10kΩ each)

ADC_VCOIL: Coil voltage sensing via resistor divider (R10/R11: 10kΩ each)

RGB LED (19-337C) for status indication with current limiting resistors (R: 750Ω, G: 150Ω, B: 200Ω)

2.4 Connectors
J2: 3-pin programming header (5V, GND, RESET_UPDI)

J3: 3-pin coil connection (one lead across pins 1&2, one lead on pin 3)

